// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Windows Defender Context Menu Removed
// Sigma ID: b9e8c7d6-a5f4-4e3d-8b1a-9f0c8d7e6a5b
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Matt Anderson (Huntress)
// Date: 2025-07-09 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: defense-impairment, T1685
// Description: Detects the use of reg.exe or PowerShell to delete the Windows Defender context menu handler
//   registry keys. This action removes the "Scan with Microsoft Defender" option from the right-
//   click menu for files, directories, and drives. Attackers may use this technique to hinder
//   manual, on-demand scans and reduce the visibility of the security product.
// False positives:
//   - May be part of a system customization or "debloating" script, but this is highly unusual in a managed corporate environment.
// References:
//   - https://research.splunk.com/endpoint/395ed5fe-ad13-4366-9405-a228427bdd91/
//   - https://winaero.com/how-to-delete-scan-with-windows-defender-from-context-menu-in-windows-10/
//   - https://thedfirreport.com/2021/10/18/icedid-to-xinglocker-ransomware-in-24-hours/
//   - https://www.threatdown.com/blog/lazyscripter-from-empire-to-double-rat/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_defender_remove_context_menu.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ((FolderPath endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\reg.exe") or (ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName in~ ("powershell_ise.EXE", "PowerShell.EXE", "pwsh.dll", "reg.exe"))) and (ProcessCommandLine contains "del" or ProcessCommandLine contains "Remove-Item" or ProcessCommandLine contains "ri ") and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\shellex\\ContextMenuHandlers\\EPP"
